## SQ-WT-03 | carry-over: Common's [wandering_trader] becomes Loot's new config file
@group A (full pack, fixture toml)
@commands before boot put `old_common_bees_trader.toml` as `config/creativecommon-common.toml`, no `creativeloot-common.toml`; boot; read both files and the log
@pass `config/creativeloot-common.toml` has `[wandering_trader]` enabled = true, traderIntervalTicks = 48000, commonTrades = 12, rareTrades = 3; Common's file has no `[wandering_trader]` after the boot; latest.log has `[swaps] config sections [wandering_trader] carried over from creativecommon-common.toml to creativeloot-common.toml`
@fails the carry in `CreativeLoot` constructor (before `registerConfig`); Common still declaring the section
@draft fixture copy as a section `@@prep run`; first runner writes the steps
@modset none
## SQ-WT-04 | trader offer counts and spawn wait read from Loot's config; vanilla defaults without the pack values
@group A
@commands full pack: `/summon minecraft:wandering_trader ~ ~ ~`; `/data get entity @e[type=minecraft:wandering_trader,limit=1,sort=nearest] Offers.Recipes` and count; then `qrun.py toml config/creativeloot-common.toml wandering_trader enabled false`, wait for the reload, summon a second trader and count; on `@modset cc_only alone` plus Creative Loot, read the generated `config/creativeloot-common.toml`
@pass pack values: about 25 common + 5 rare offers (fewer only when a pool is smaller); enabled false: 5 + 1; the generated file has enabled = false, 24000 / 5 / 1; latest.log has no mixin apply error naming `WanderingTrader`
@fails `creativeloot.mixins.json` missing the two mixins; `LootConfig` not registered; Common's old mixins still listed in `creativecommon.mixins.json` (double apply)
@draft the second half needs a Loot-plus-Common modset (no manifest yet; `qmodset.py` can add one)
@modset none
